  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is shown to interact with P2X purinoceptors, which are ionotropic receptors that mediate cellular signaling through purine ligand binding. This interaction is consistent across three distinct paths, all pointing to the same target compound [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which is identified as a modulator of BL-41. The shared mechanism of action—targeting a common receptor—suggests a potential for cross-pathway relevance, though the specific role of each P2X receptor in BL-41 modulation remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Mollicellin N and BL-41 through a common intermediary, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism of action and the functional significance of the observed interactions.",
